    },
    {
      "id": "_lapxqR5mEkRnEVtXv1ju",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -31639.098311239864,
      "y": -5083.370502767046,
      "width": 1600.098876953125,
      "height": 225,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aC",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2058168884,
      "version": 547,
      "versionNonce": 144989492,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1784122192758,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "How to scale to large nos of videos uploaded/watched a day?\n- Video service is stateless, easily scale horizontally with LB\n- Video Metadata either Cassandra or DynamoDB easily scalable and reliable using replication, partition by videoId, handle popular videos hot partition using caches\n- Video Processing Service - add more parallel processing nodes\n- S3 scales easily also have CDNs(cache both segments and manifest files) for popular videos\n\n\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "How to scale to large nos of videos uploaded/watched a day?\n- Video service is stateless, easily scale horizontally with LB\n- Video Metadata either Cassandra or DynamoDB easily scalable and reliable using replication, partition by videoId, handle popular videos hot partition using caches\n- Video Processing Service - add more parallel processing nodes\n- S3 scales easily also have CDNs(cache both segments and manifest files) for popular videos\n\n\n\n",
